{"name":"Monument","hex":"#84898c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Monument","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A place in the United States:\nA town in El Paso County, Colorado.\nAn unincorporated community in Logan County, Kansas.\nA census-designated place in Lea County, New Mexico.\nA minor city in Grant County, Oregon.\nA census-designated place in Liberty Township, Centre County, Pennsylvania.","A town in El Paso County, Colorado."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of the five most prestigious men's one-day road cycling races: Milan–San Remo, Tour of Flanders, Paris–Roubaix, Liege–Bastogne–Liege and Giro di Lombardia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Monument"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monument","blocks":[{"text":"A monument is a type of structure created to commemorate a person or event, or which has become relevant to a social group as a part of their remembrance of historic times, or cultural heritage, due to its artistic, historical, political, technical or architectural importance. Examples of monuments include statues, (war) memorials, historical buildings, and cultural assets. If there is a public interest in its preservation, a monument can for example be listed as a UNESCO World Heritage Site."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dc/Monumento_ao_Cristo_Redentor.jpg/330px-Monumento_ao_Cristo_Redentor.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monument","wikidata":"Q4989906"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Monumento_a_la_Bandera_2.jpg/500px-Monumento_a_la_Bandera_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Monumento_a_la_Bandera_2.jpg/1280px-Monumento_a_la_Bandera_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thum